      {
        "heading": "5  |  Interpretation and limitations",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "list_item",
            "text": "Income: Cuba ranks lowest on the median household income point estimate, with its largest gap relative to Sandoval County."
          },
          {
            "type": "list_item",
            "text": "Heating: Cuba’s fuel profile resembles the statewide electric-heating share more closely than the county’s, while the county has the highest gas-heating share."
          },
          {
            "type": "list_item",
            "text": "Uncertainty: Cuba has only 159 estimated occupied housing units. Its B19013 median income has a 90% margin of error of approximately ±$46,069; apparent differences may not be statistically significant."
          },
          {
            "type": "list_item",
            "text": "Geography: Cuba refers to the incorporated village (Census place), not ZIP code 87013. ZIP Code Tabulation Areas are different geographic units."
          },
          {
            "type": "list_item",
            "text": "Scope: B25040 identifies primary heating fuel—not system efficiency, household energy use, fuel cost, or access to infrastructure. These results do not prove that income causes fuel choices."
          }
        ]
      },
